<section class="section reveal" id="classes-basics">
  <span class="section-label">Core Concepts</span>
  <h2>Defining Classes and Objects</h2>

  <p>A class defines the structure and behavior of objects. Think of it as a template. An object is an instance of that template — a concrete example with its own state. The <code>__init__</code> method is the constructor, called when you create a new instance.</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">ImageClassifier</span>:
    <span class="st">"""A neural network classifier for images.

    Attributes:
        model_name (str): Architecture name
        accuracy (float): Validation accuracy
        is_trained (bool): Training status
    """</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">model_name</span>: <span class="fn">str</span>):
        <span class="st">"""Initialize classifier."""</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">model_name</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">model_name</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">accuracy</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">0.0</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">is_trained</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">False</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">train</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">epochs</span>: <span class="fn">int</span>) <span class="op">-></span> <span class="kw">None</span>:
        <span class="st">"""Train the model."""</span>
        <span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="st">f"Training </span>{<span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">model_name</span>}<span class="st">..."</span>)
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">accuracy</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">0.92</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">is_trained</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="kw">True</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">predict</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">image</span>: <span class="fn">str</span>) <span class="op">-></span> <span class="fn">str</span>:
        <span class="st">"""Make a prediction."""</span>
        <span class="kw">if</span> <span class="kw">not</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">is_trained</span>:
            <span class="kw">raise</span> <span class="fn">RuntimeError</span>(<span class="st">"Train first"</span>)
        <span class="kw">return</span> <span class="st">"cat"</span>

<span class="cm"># Create an instance</span>
<span class="va">classifier</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">ImageClassifier</span>(<span class="st">"ResNet50"</span>)
<span class="va">classifier</span>.<span class="fn">train</span>(<span class="nm">10</span>)
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="va">classifier</span>.<span class="va">accuracy</span>)  <span class="cm"># 0.92</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> We define a class with <code>__init__</code> that initializes three attributes. Methods like <code>train()</code> and <code>predict()</code> operate on these attributes via <code>self</code>. When we create an instance, <code>__init__</code> runs automatically. We then call methods and access attributes using dot notation.</p>
  </div>

  <h3>Instance vs Class Attributes</h3>
  <p>Instance attributes are unique to each object. Class attributes are shared by all instances of that class:</p>

  <div class="code-header"><span class="code-lang">Python</span><button class="copy-btn">Copy</button></div>
  <pre><code><span class="kw">class</span> <span class="fn">DataLoader</span>:
    <span class="cm"># Class attribute — shared</span>
    <span class="va">default_batch_size</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="nm">32</span>

    <span class="kw">def</span> <span class="fn">__init__</span>(<span class="va">self</span>, <span class="va">data</span>, <span class="va">batch_size</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="kw">None</span>):
        <span class="cm"># Instance attributes — per object</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">data</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">data</span>
        <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="va">batch_size</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="va">batch_size</span> <span class="op">or</span> <span class="va">self</span>.<span class="fn">default_batch_size</span>

<span class="va">loader1</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">DataLoader</span>([<span class="nm">1</span>, <span class="nm">2</span>, <span class="nm">3</span>])
<span class="va">loader2</span> <span class="op">=</span> <span class="fn">DataLoader</span>([<span class="nm">4</span>, <span class="nm">5</span>, <span class="nm">6</span>], <span class="va">batch_size</span><span class="op">=</span><span class="nm">16</span>)

<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="va">loader1</span>.<span class="va">batch_size</span>)  <span class="cm"># 32 (default)</span>
<span class="fn">print</span>(<span class="va">loader2</span>.<span class="va">batch_size</span>)  <span class="cm"># 16 (custom)</span></code></pre>
  <div class="code-explain">
    <p><strong>What is happening here:</strong> <code>default_batch_size</code> is a class attribute shared across all instances. Each instance can have its own <code>batch_size</code> value, overriding or using the class default.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="key-takeaway">
    <h4>✦ Key Takeaways</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Classes are templates; objects are instances of templates</li>
      <li>The <code>__init__</code> constructor initializes instance attributes</li>
      <li>Methods are functions attached to a class, with <code>self</code> as first parameter</li>
      <li>Instance attributes are unique per object; class attributes are shared</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

